.\" tests/test_man.sh checks that every option and parameter pond knows is here.
.TH POND 1 2026-10-28 "pond 0.38" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pond \- dispersive water waves in a basin, drawn in 3\-D, with sound
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pond
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B pond \-\-script
.I file
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B pond \-\-list\-params
.br
.B pond \-\-write\-config
.RI [ file ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pond
solves the linear water\-wave equations with gravity, surface tension, depth
and viscous damping on a rectangular or round basin, from a 30 cm tray to an
80 m sea, and draws the surface in 3\-D: refraction, caustics on the floor,
reflections, a sky and a sun.
Sources are drops, rain, a breeze in gusts, a wind sea, a wavemaker on a
wall, a boat with its Kelvin wake, floats, vertical shaking (Faraday waves)
and sideways jolts (the seiche); an optional nonlinear correction (HOS)
sharpens the crests.
The sound is synthesised from the same events.
.PP
Everything that can change while it runs is a named
.IR parameter :
keys nudge them, the command line and the configuration file set them, and
scripts change them over time.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Before the program starts
.TP
.BI \-\-grid " N"
The mode grid, a power of two (default 512; 256 in the browser).
.TP
.BI \-\-window " WxH"
Window size in pixels (default 1280x800); one number means 16:10.
.TP
.B \-\-2d
Top\-down CPU renderer instead of the 3\-D view; needs no OpenGL.
.TP
.B \-\-nomsaa
Do not ask for a multisampled framebuffer (for displays where window
creation fails).
.TP
.B \-\-cpu\-caustics
Compute the caustic light map on the CPU (default: on the GPU when possible).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-audio
Open no sound device at all.
.B \-\-mute
keeps the device open but silent.
.TP
.BI \-\-hos\-nc " N"
Modes per axis in the nonlinear correction (default 64).
.TP
.BI \-\-hos\-order " M"
Order of the nonlinear correction (default 3).
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " N"
Start with preset 1 to 4: tray 30 cm, pond 3 m, pool 12 m, sea 80 m.
.TP
.BR \-\-shape " rect|disk"
The basin's shape.
.TP
.BI \-\-basin " WxL"
The basin's width and length in metres; one number for a square, or a
disk's diameter.
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " H"
Water depth in metres.
.SS Parameters
Every parameter (see
.BR PARAMETERS )
is an option:
\fB\-\-\fIname value\fR,
or for a boolean
\fB\-\-\fIname\fR
to turn it on and
\fB\-\-no\-\fIname\fR
to turn it off.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-params
Print every parameter with its current value, range and meaning, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-scene " S"
Sources already on: any of
.BR rain ,
.BR paddle ,
.BR breeze ,
comma\-separated.
.TP
.BI \-\-cam " Y,P,D"
Camera yaw and pitch in degrees, distance in basin lengths.
.TP
.BI \-\-sound " K=V,..."
The five sound levels
.RB ( drops ,
.BR bed ,
.BR brown ,
.BR breeze ,
.BR harsh ;
1 is as designed).
.TP
.B \-\-hos
The nonlinear correction on (the parameter
.BR nonlinear ).
.SS Per run
.TP
.BI \-\-script " file"
Run a script (see
.BR SCRIPTS ).
.TP
.BI \-\-frames " N"
Quit after
.I N
displayed frames.
.TP
.BI \-\-snap3d " file"
With
.BR \-\-frames ,
save the last 3\-D frame as a BMP.
.TP
.BI \-\-bench " N"
Run
.I N
headless frames of the CPU path, print timings, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-snap " file"
With
.BR \-\-bench ,
save the last frame as a BMP.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Read
.I file
instead of the default configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-config
Read no configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-\-write\-config " [\fIfile\fR]"
Write the settings as they stand, after the other options, as a
configuration file (by default the first location in
.BR FILES ),
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the keys and options, and exit.
.SH PARAMETERS
Booleans take on/off, yes/no, true/false or 1/0; enumerations take their
names or a number; reals are clamped to their range and accept
.BR % .
.B pond \-\-list\-params
prints the current values.
.SS The basin
.TP
.BR preset " tray|pond|pool|sea"
Sets size, depth, floor and camera together.
.TP
.BR shape " rect|disk"
Rectangle or disk.
.TP
.BR width ", " length
Metres, 0.05 to 1000 (a disk's diameter is its width).
.TP
.B depth
Water depth, metres, 0.002 to 5000.
.TP
.B nonlinear
The HOS correction (rectangle only).
.TP
.B damping
Extra uniform damping, 1/s.
.TP
.B warp
Simulated seconds per real second, 1/64 to 64.
.SS Sources
.TP
.BR rain ", " rain\-rate
Rain on; drops per simulated second.
.TP
.B drop\-size
A raindrop's crater width in metres (0: 2 cm, or a few grid cells on a
coarse grid); a click is twice it.
.TP
.BR breeze ", " breeze\-gain ", " gusts
A wind sea on; a multiplier on its forcing; whether it comes in drifting
gusts (cat's paws).
.TP
.B wind
Wind speed, m/s, 0 to 30: a fetch\-limited sea over the basin's length
(0: the breeze's own settings).
.TP
.BR boat ", " boat\-speed
A boat driving round the basin; its speed as a Froude number (0.4 is a
dinghy under way).
.TP
.B floats
How many floats ride the surface, 0 to 12.
.TP
.BR shake ", " shake\-amp ", " shake\-freq
Vertical shaking, its acceleration in g and its frequency in Hz; Faraday
waves answer at half the frequency.
.TP
.B finger\-gain
A multiplier on the drag\-a\-finger forcing.
.TP
.BR paddle ", " paddle\-freq ", " paddle\-stroke
The wavemaker, its frequency in Hz (held inside the band the basin can
answer), and a multiplier on its speed.
.TP
.BR paddle\-wall " x=0|x=Lx|y=0|y=Ly"
Which wall it stands on (the disk: the rim).
.TP
.BR paddle\-pos ", " paddle\-span
Where along the wall, and how much of it, both 0 to 1.
.TP
.B paddle\-mark
Outline the wavemaker on the water.
.SS The picture
.TP
.BR glass " opaque|floor|glass|glass+bottom|none"
The container.
.TP
.BR floor " tiles|checker|sand"
The floor pattern.
.TP
.BR look " animation|video"
A clean render, or the water as a camera films it: exposure, film tone,
bloom, lens, grain, a hand\-held drift, clouds, ripples, glitter, and the
garden moving in the wind.
.TP
.BR setting " none|house"
Nothing round the basin, or a house, terrace and garden (basins 4 to 40 m).
.TP
.B gain
Display gain on the wave height.
.TP
.BR sun\-elev ", " sun\-azim
The sun's elevation and azimuth, degrees; below \-6 it is night and the
moon lights the water.
.TP
.BR yaw ", " pitch ", " dist
Camera yaw and pitch in degrees, distance in basin lengths.
.TP
.BR cam\-x ", " cam\-z
What the camera looks at, from the basin's centre, \-0.5 to 0.5 of its
width and length.
.TP
.BR hud ", " help ", " fullscreen ", " paused ", " view
The settings box; the help panel; full screen; time stopped; in
.BR \-\-2d ,
a height map instead of the rendered view.
.SS Sound
.TP
.BR volume ", " mute
Master volume 0 to 1; silent with the device kept open.
.TP
.BR sound.drops ", " sound.bed ", " sound.brown ", " sound.breeze ", " sound.harsh
Drop plinks, the rain bed, brown noise, the breeze, and the gusts and rustle
in it; 0 to 4, 1 as designed.
.SH KEYS
Lower case nudges a parameter down and upper case (shift) up, unless a pair
is listed.
.B h
shows this list in the window.
No function keys are needed.
.SS Camera
.PD 0
.TP 14
arrows
Orbit (held; shift faster, ctrl or cmd finer); also keypad 4 6 8 2.
.TP
alt+up/down
Zoom (held); also PgUp, PgDn, the wheel, a pinch.
.TP
.BR o ", Home"
Reset the camera.
.SS Basin
.TP 14
.B 1 2 3 4
Presets: tray, pond, pool, sea.
.TP
.B n
Rectangle or disk.
.TP
.BR "[ ]" " / " "{ }"
Width, length (5% a press).
.TP
.BR ", ." " / " \e
Depth; make it square again, keeping the area.
.TP
.B y
Nonlinear correction.
.TP
.BR "\- =" ", " x / X
Time warp; damping.
.TP
.BR g / G ", " f
Display gain; floor pattern.
.TP
.B t
Container: opaque, floor, glass, glass+bottom, none.
.TP
.B \(ga
Setting: none or the house.
.TP
.B Tab
Look: animation or video.
.SS Sources
.TP 14
.BR r ", " i / I
Rain; rain rate.
.TP
.B b
Breeze.
.TP
.BR w / W
Wind.
.TP
.BR e ", " z / Z
Boat; its speed.
.TP
.BR E " / " C
One more float; clear them.
.TP
.BR ; ", " \(aq/\(dq ", " //?
Shake (Faraday); its amplitude; its frequency.
.TP
.BR 0 " / " )
Jolt along x, along y (alt: three times harder).
.TP
.BR 5 " / " % ", " 6 " / " ^
The sun lower / higher; round, and back.
.TP
.BR p " / " P
Wavemaker on or off; next wall.
.TP
.BR k / K ", " l / L
Its frequency; its span.
.TP
.BR "< >"
Slide it along the wall.
.TP
.B D
Its outline on the water.
.SS Sound
.TP 14
.BR m ", " a / A
Sound on or off; volume.
.TP
.BR j / J ", " u / U
Drop plinks; rain bed.
.TP
.B 7 8 9
Brown noise, breeze, harshness (shift: up).
.SS Other
.TP 14
.B d
Hide or show the settings box.
.TP
alt+enter
Full screen.
.TP
.BR c ", " C
Clear the water; clear the floats.
.TP
space
Pause.
.TP
.B s
Screenshot (pond\-NNN.bmp in the current directory).
.TP
.BR h ", " esc ", " q
Help; back out one layer (script, full screen, program); quit.
.PD
.SS Mouse and touch
Click on the water for a drop, shift\-click for a big one; drag on it to
push a finger through it.
Drag off the water, or with the right button, or ctrl+drag, to orbit; the
wheel zooms.
On a touch screen two fingers orbit and pinch to zoom.
.SH SCRIPTS
A script is a configuration file with a time axis: one event per line, a
time and then parameter settings.
.PP
.nf
.RS
at 0     clear  preset pool  rain on  rain\-rate 1.5
at 0     camera 35,42,1.5
at 0     say "a pool in the rain"
at 2     yaw += 90 over 30
+8       paddle on  paddle\-freq 2.4 over 8
at 60    loop
.RE
.fi
.PP
.BI at " T"
is seconds from the start,
.BI + T
seconds after the line before, and a line with no time shares the previous
line's.
Times are wall\-clock, so a script may change
.B warp
itself.
Every parameter name is a verb; a value may be absolute or relative
.RB ( += ,
.BR \-= ),
and a number may take
.BI over " T"
to get there smoothly.
The other verbs:
.TP
.BR drop " \fIX,Y\fR [\fISIZE\fR] | " "drop random"
A drop at fractions of the basin.
.TP
.BI jolt " DUX,DUY"
Shove the basin sideways, m/s.
.TP
.BI boat " X,Y\fR[\fP,HEADING\fR]"
Put the boat there (fractions of the basin, degrees from +x) and start it.
.TP
.BR float " \fIX,Y\fR | " "float random"
One more float.
.TP
.BI camera " Y,P,D " \fR[ "over T" \fR]
Move the camera.
.TP
.BI say " \(dqtext\(dq"
A caption under the settings box (also
.BR caption ).
.TP
.B clear
Calm the water.
.TP
.BR loop ", " end
Start again; stop (also
.BR stop ).
.PP
.B #
starts a comment.
A key on a parameter the script is moving takes that parameter over; the
script carries on with the rest.
.B esc
stops the script.
.SH FILES
The configuration file is the first of these that exists:
.IP
.nf
$POND_CONFIG
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pond/pond.conf
~/.config/pond/pond.conf
~/.pondrc
\&./pond.conf
.fi
.PP
One
.I key
=
.I value
per line (also
.IB key : " value"
or
.IR "key value" );
the keys are the parameters and the start\-up options above;
.B #
and
.B ;
start comments;
.B \-
and
.B _
are the same in a key.
Unknown keys are reported with their line number and skipped.
Settings are read as built\-in defaults, then the file, then the command line.
.PP
.I demos/*.pond
in the source tree: twelve scripts, from a three\-minute tour to a
ten\-minute showcase of everything.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B POND_CONFIG
The configuration file to read before the usual places.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where
.I pond/pond.conf
is looked for (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.TP
.B POND_WAV
Record what is heard to this WAV file.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
pond \-\-preset 3 \-\-scene breeze \-\-setting house \-\-look video
pond \-\-shape disk \-\-basin 10 \-\-paddle \-\-paddle\-freq 1.2
pond \-\-preset 4 \-\-wind 12 \-\-boat
pond \-\-preset 2 \-\-shake \-\-shake\-freq 3
pond \-\-script demos/showcase.pond \-\-fullscreen \-\-no\-hud
pond \-\-volume 0.3 \-\-glass floor \-\-write\-config
pond \-\-frames 120 \-\-snap3d shot.bmp
.fi
